.TH DOTS 1 "2026-09-28" "hvpaiva/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dots \- keep this machine's personal layer in sync with hvpaiva/dotfiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dots
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dots
fronts the three repositories that make up a machine's personal layer on top of
Omarchy, so a change never has to be routed by hand to the right one:
.TP
.B dotfiles
.IR ~/.dotfiles ,
a bare repository whose work tree is
.IR $HOME .
Tracked files sit exactly where the programs read them, with no symlinks.
.I ~/.gitignore
is a whitelist: everything is ignored unless listed, so only files inside that
boundary are ever reported, new ones included.
.TP
.B private
.IR ~/.local/share/dotfiles-private ,
the sensitive per-host files (identities, internal endpoints), symlinked into
place from
.IR hosts/<host>/ .
.TP
.B nvim
.IR ~/.config/nvim ,
the editor configuration, recorded in dotfiles as a submodule pointer so a clone
cannot forget it.
.PP
Non-sensitive per-host files live in the dotfiles repo under
.I ~/.config/dotfiles/hosts/<host>/
and are symlinked the same way. Which host a machine is comes from
.IR ~/.config/dotfiles/host .
When a program replaces one of those links with a regular file (omarchy-shell
rewrites shell.json, the monitor panel rewrites monitors.lua), the live file
wins:
.B save
and
.B update
copy it back into its tree, restore the link and report it as a change.
.PP
.IR README.md ,
.I bootstrap.sh
and
.I .github/
are tracked at the repository root, where GitHub expects them, and kept out of
.I $HOME
by a sparse checkout; see
.BR root .
.PP
Output follows the kubectl convention: tables with a header row, one object per
row, state words coloured by meaning when standard output is a terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR status " [" -f "|" --fetch "] [" -o "|" --offline ]
The default. Three tables and one line. REPO: branch, local changes, origin
state (in sync, N to push, N behind, diverged). The commit dotfiles records for
nvim is a dotfiles file: a live nvim commit it does not have yet counts as a
dotfiles change, and nvim not yet on the recorded commit shows as behind
record. PATH: every changed or new file inside the tracked
boundary and the repo it belongs to. HOST: the per-host links and how many of
the local checks of
.B doctor
warn. Origin is fetched at most once every ten minutes;
.B \-f
fetches now,
.B \-o
does not fetch.
.TP
.BR diff " [" "git diff arguments" ]
The changes themselves, every repo: git diff for tracked files, then the new
files inside the boundary.
.TP
.B check
Run CI's ShellCheck, shell/Ruby syntax, executable-bit checks, dotfiles unit
tests and shell tests (.config/bash/tests) against a temporary copy of what save
would commit, including new files and sparse root entries. Requires shellcheck,
ruby and bats; a shell test skips what needs a tool the machine lacks (tmux,
ble.sh, rich-ri...). Leaves the real index and work tree unchanged. Covers
public dotfiles; private and nvim retain their own repository hooks. Container
tests remain in CI.
.TP
.BR save " [" \-m " \fIMESSAGE\fR] [" \-n "|" \-\-no\-push ]
Commit and push every change, in every repo, in this order: nvim, private,
dotfiles. The live nvim commit is recorded in dotfiles first when it moved
forward; replaced per-host links are adopted first. A message is asked per repo
on a terminal, with one proposed from the changed files;
.B \-m
uses the same message everywhere;
.B \-n
commits without pushing.
After adopting per-host files, runs check before any commit or push. Failed
checks or missing tools stop the save with a nonzero status, even with
.BR \-n .
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-quick ]
Bring the machine up to date: fast-forward every repo to origin (local edits
are stashed around the merge and restored), re-link the per-host files, install
the mise tools the configuration lists but the machine lacks, then upgrade the
mise tools, rebuild augur when its clone moved past the last build (shells
already open keep the engine they started until
.BR "ble\-augur restart" ),
update Ollama on Ubuntu, where its own installer put it, and pull the model
augur asks by default, rebuild bashdb when bash moved to a new release, update
ble.sh (shells already open keep the version they loaded until
.BR ble\-reload )
and update the tmux plugins.
.B \-\-quick
stops after the missing tools.
.TP
.B push
Push the commits that are not on origin yet, in every repo, without committing.
A repo whose origin moved is left alone.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the machine against the intended state and print one row per check:
each repo (changes, origin, nvim record), host marker, per-host links, root
entries, git identity and hooks, Omarchy (and on Arch the pacman hook that
records installs), build dependencies, mise (the official build in ~/.local/bin,
every tool installed), rust, augur, Ollama and augur's model when Ollama is
installed, ble.sh, bashdb, tmux version and plugins, distro copies of tools
the layer replaces, processes still running a removed binary, font, themes,
kubectl completion, a real login shell (starts clean, PAGER=less, dots on PATH)
and GitHub over SSH. Exit status is 1 when any check warns.
.TP
.BR setup " [" \-\-host " \fINAME\fR] [" \-\-reset "] [" \-\-skip\-omarchy "] [" \-\-skip\-private "] [" \-\-skip\-mise "] [" \-\-skip\-rust ]
Install or repair the whole layer; what
.I bootstrap.sh
runs after the clone. Idempotent: every step checks before acting. Steps, in
order: build dependencies (sudo); Omarchy, which on Ubuntu means the
omarchy-ubuntu bootstrap; the dotfiles repo (remotes, sparse checkout,
fast-forward); host marker; private layer (needs GitHub over SSH, skipped with
a warning otherwise); per-host links; neovim config; distro packages the layer
replaces (sudo); the pacman hook (Arch, sudo); rustup; augur; ble.sh; bashdb;
tmux plugins; mise and every tool in mise/config.toml; terminal font; themes;
kubectl completion. Then
.B doctor
and a summary. Everything printed is also appended to
.IR ~/.local/state/dotfiles/setup.log .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " NAME"
Which
.I hosts/NAME
layers this machine uses. Asked once on a terminal otherwise, and kept in
.IR ~/.config/dotfiles/host .
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Drop local edits to tracked dotfiles and private files (hard reset to origin).
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-omarchy
Leave Omarchy alone: port bootstrap, font and themes.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-private
Do not touch the private layer.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-mise
Do not install mise or its tools.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-rust
Do not install rustup or augur.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-secrets
Do not touch 1Password, gh, the SSH key or Tailscale.
.RE
.PP
sudo asks for the password once and its credential is kept alive for the run.
.PP
Secrets: unlock 1Password once (the app, with CLI integration on) and
.B setup
does the logins itself from the item
.I op://Private/dots
in the account my.1password.com (DOTS_OP_ITEM and DOTS_OP_ACCOUNT override
them): field
.I github-token
logs gh in; this machine's SSH key is generated when missing and added to GitHub
for authentication and signing, so nothing asks again afterwards;
.I tailscale-auth-key
connects Tailscale;
.I cloudflare-token
writes the token file. A missing field is reported, never fatal.
.RS
.RE
.TP
.BR root " show|hide"
.B show
puts README.md, bootstrap.sh and .github/ in
.I $HOME
to edit them;
.B hide
takes them out again; a modified one has to be saved first.
.TP
.BR clean " [\-\-all] [\-y]"
List the backups
.BR setup ", bootstrap.sh and the Ubuntu port move aside instead of deleting:"
the files the
first checkout would have overwritten, a ~/.config/nvim that was not a git
clone, the *.bak-omarchy copies the port keeps and the folders of a migration by
hand. With
.B \-\-all
remove them after one confirmation;
.B \-y
skips the question (required without a terminal). Logs are never touched.
While some exist,
.B status
shows them in a BACKUPS column.
.TP
.BR private " \fIgit arguments\fR"
Run git in the private repo.
.TP
.BR nvim " \fIgit arguments\fR"
Run git in the nvim repo.
.TP
.BR git " \fIgit arguments\fR"
Run git in the dotfiles repo. Any command
.B dots
does not know is passed to git there as well, so
.B dots log
and
.B dots add \-p
work as expected.
.TP
.BR help " [" command ]
Built-in documentation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dotfiles
The bare dotfiles repository.
.TP
.I ~/.dotfiles/info/sparse-checkout
The patterns that keep the root entries out of $HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.gitignore
The whitelist of tracked paths.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dotfiles/host
This machine's host name for the per-host layers.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dotfiles/hosts/<host>/
Public per-host files, symlinked into $HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dotfiles-private/{hosts/<host>,common}/
Private per-host and shared files, symlinked into $HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dotfiles/
Logs (setup.log, mise-install.log, mise-upgrade.log, augur-build.log,
ollama-update.log, ollama-pull.log, blesh-update.log), the commit of the last
augur build (augur-built) and what
was moved aside instead of deleted (pre-checkout-*, nvim-*), listed by
.BR clean .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR DOTFILES_REPO ", " DOTFILES_PUSH_URL ", " DOTFILES_BRANCH ", " DOTFILES_PRIVATE_REPO
Override the repositories; used by the container test.
.TP
.B DOTS_OS_RELEASE
An os-release file to read instead of /etc/os-release; used by the unit tests.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 when
.B doctor
finds something to look at, when a repository cannot be fast-forwarded, or on
any error. git commands passed through return git's status.
.SH EXAMPLES
A first machine:
.PP
.nf
    bash <(curl \-fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hvpaiva/dotfiles/main/bootstrap.sh)
.fi
.PP
A day: edit a file where its program reads it, then
.PP
.nf
    dots            # see it listed under PATH, with its repo
    dots save       # commit and push it
    dots update     # on the other machine
.fi
.PP
Add a tool for every machine: put it in
.I ~/.config/mise/config.toml
and run
.B dots update
on each machine.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR mise (1),
.BR omarchy\-update (1)
.PP
The README at https://github.com/hvpaiva/dotfiles explains the layout and the
decisions behind it.
